cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use lintlang in your research or tooling, please cite it."
title: "lintlang: Static linter for AI agent configs, tool descriptions, and system prompts"
version: "0.3.0"
date-released: "2026-06-07"
authors:
  - name: "Hermes Labs"
    email: rbosch@lpci.ai
url: "https://github.com/hermes-labs-ai/lintlang"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hermes-labs-ai/lintlang"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >
  lintlang is a zero-LLM static linter for AI agent configurations, tool descriptions,
  and system prompts. It combines HERM v1.1 dimensional scoring (6 dimensions,
  8 signal categories) with 7 structural detectors (H1-H7) and pipeline detectors
  (P1-P3) that catch language-level failures — vague instructions, missing constraints,
  uncalibrated thresholds — before they reach runtime. Deterministic, 0 LLM calls
  per default scan, ~2ms per file.
keywords:
  - AI agents
  - static analysis
  - prompt engineering
  - linter
  - agent configuration
  - LLM reliability
